(2. The main feeder cable shall be 3.5 core 300 sq.mm.) Tj T*
(3. The cables shall be suitable for a maximum continuous conductor temperature of 90 deg C.) Tj T*
(Control cables shall be PVC insulated, copper conductor of 2.5 sq.mm, 1.1 kV grade, conforming) Tj T*
(to IS 1554 \(Part 1\).) Tj T*
(4. Conductors shall be stranded, class 2, conforming to IS 8130. Cables shall be laid in RCC) Tj T*
(trenches or on perforated cable trays as shown in the drawings.) Tj T*
(5. Cable ends shall be terminated using double compression glands and crimped lugs.) Tj T*
(6. Each drum shall be marked with the manufacturer's name, size, voltage grade and year of) Tj T*
(manufacture.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(SECTION 6: TESTING, INSPECTION AND CERTIFICATION) Tj T*
(1. Pumps shall be tested at the works in accordance with IS 9137. Pumps shall bear the ISI) Tj T*
(mark.) Tj T*
(2. Routine tests on motors shall be carried out as per IS 4029.) Tj T*
(3. Motors shall bear the ISI mark.) Tj T*
(4. Cables shall be tested in accordance with IS 10810.) Tj T*
(5. Routine test certificates of cables shall be furnished with each consignment. The equipment) Tj T*
(shall be inspected by the Engineer-in-charge at the manufacturer's works before dispatch.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(7 DOCUMENTATION, WARRANTY AND TRAINING) Tj T*
(1. The contractor shall submit detailed shop drawings for approval within 21 days of award of) Tj T*
(work.) Tj T*
(2. Three sets of operation and maintenance manuals shall be handed over on completion.) Tj T*
(3. The complete installation shall be guaranteed against defective design, material and) Tj T*
(workmanship for a period of 12 months from the date of handing over.) Tj T*
(4. The contractor shall train the Department's operating staff in operation and routine) Tj T*
(maintenance.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
